.TH KACLAIG 1 "November 2026" "kaclaig 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kaclaig \- generate Keep a Changelog entries from git history using an LLM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kaclaig
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kaclaig
reads the git log and diff between the current state and the latest parent tag,
combines them with the existing changelog, and asks an OpenAI-compatible LLM to
write a new Keep a Changelog 1.1.0 entry.
.PP
The generated entry is validated. If it is invalid, the reason is sent back to
the LLM and it retries.
.PP
By default the entry is printed to stdout and no file is modified. Use
.B \-w
to write it into the changelog file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-major
Bump the major version segment (ignored with \fB\-\-new-version\fR).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-minor
Bump the minor version segment, resetting patch (ignored with \fB\-\-new-version\fR).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-patch
Bump the patch version segment (ignored with \fB\-\-new-version\fR).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-unreleased
Generate an \fB[Unreleased]\fR entry instead of a release. This is the default.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-semver\-check
Enable the semver conformance check for release bumps. It is off by default.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-new-version " " \fITAG\fR
New version or tag to generate. Overrides the bump flags. By default the
version is derived from the latest tag.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-from " " \fITAG\fR
Previous tag to diff against. Defaults to the latest parent tag.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-changelog " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to the changelog file. Auto-detected when omitted.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to an opencode-style LLM config file (\fBopencode.json\fR format).
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-config\-blob " " \fIJSON\fR
Inline LLM config JSON blob, in the same format as \fB\-\-config\fR. It takes
precedence over \fB\-\-config\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Git repository directory. Defaults to the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-write
Update the changelog file instead of only printing the generated entry.
When a section for the same version already exists, its entries are merged:
existing lines are kept and only identical bullets are listed once.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print progress and validation attempts to stderr.
.SH LLM CONFIGURATION
Connection settings are resolved in this order:
.IP 1. 4
the \fB\-C\fR / \fB\-\-config\-blob\fR inline JSON,
.IP 2. 4
the \fB\-c\fR / \fB\-\-config\fR file,
.IP 3. 4
\fB$HOME/.kaclaig\-llm/kaclaig.json\fR,
.IP 4. 4
\fB$HOME/.config/opencode/opencode.json\fR or \fBopencode.jsonc\fR,
.IP 5. 4
environment variables (\fBLLM_MODEL\fR, \fBLLM_BASE_URL\fR,
\fBLLM_API_KEY\fR, \fBOPENAI_*\fR).
.PP
The config file uses the opencode provider format and selects the model with a
\fB<provider>/<model>\fR string:
.PP
.nf
{
  "providers": {
    "local": {
      "settings": {
        "baseURL": "https://ai.example.com/v1",
        "apiKey": "secret"
      },
      "models": { "qwen3.8-27b": { "name": "Qwen 3.8 27B" } }
    }
  },
  "model": "local/qwen3.8-27b"
}
.fi
.SH NOTES
Single-dash long option spellings, such as \fB\-major\fR or
\fB\-new-version\fR, are also accepted. Short options can be combined
(e.g. \fB\-pv\fR).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Print an \fB[Unreleased]\fR entry:
.B kaclaig
.TP
Write a patch release into the changelog:
.B kaclaig \-p \-w
.TP
Generate an explicit version against a specific parent tag:
.B kaclaig \-\-new-version 1.2.0 \-\-from v1.1.0
.TP
Pass the LLM configuration inline:
.B kaclaig \-C '{"providers":{"local":{"settings":{"baseURL":"http://localhost:11434/v1"}}},"model":"local/qwen3.8-27b"}'
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.kaclaig-llm/kaclaig.json
Default LLM configuration file.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/opencode/opencode.json
Fallback opencode configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README: https://github.com/kakwa/kaclaig
